# The application lives in reserva-barber/. These paths only appear at the repo
# root when `npm install` was run from the wrong directory; anchoring them with
# a leading slash keeps reserva-barber/package.json tracked as usual.
#
# DELETE THIS FILE if reserva-barber/ ever becomes the repository root. These
# anchors would then point at the project's own package.json and node_modules
# and would start ignoring them. reserva-barber/.gitignore already covers
# everything the project needs, including .mcp.json.
/node_modules/
/package.json
/package-lock.json
